WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:02.540
*Sigh*

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:04.220
That's a lot of subs.

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:06.900
But, it didn't feel right to make a video on just that.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:11.220
So, I figured let's do one last round of secrets first.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:12.320
Number one:

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:17.400
When Gael teleports in phase two, you might have noticed a tiny visual detail

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:22.680
He's actually summoning himself with a white summon soapstone, underneath you.

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.340
If you're looking for a lore explanation

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:29.340
The white summon soapstone item has always referenced the convolution of time

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:32.800
and, it's always referenced the link between undead.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:37.200
and Gael is a character that can be summoned by you all throughout the DLCs.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:41.280
So it does make some sense that he could abuse this link to your character.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:47.220
Gael, actually has quite a few little visual details that really flesh out his character

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:50.780
For instance, his soapstone messages look unlike any other.

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:56.680
and, they emanate those same skull fumes that he has all throughout phase two of his boss fight.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.560
So what are those skulls?

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:01.740
Well, there's nothing in Dark Souls 3 that defines them...

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:07.280
but they are pretty much the same as those summoned by the executioner's gloves in Bloodborne

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:10.380
Which gives us some idea what they were thinking with this asset.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:15.120
In Bloodborne, they are said to be the wrathful spirits of the past.

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:19.360
And considering they also bulge outwards from the purging monument...

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:26.620
I think it's fair to say that Gael, who has probably consumed half the souls of the world, by this point,

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:32.520
it's fair to say that he is overflowing with the spirits and the curses of the past as well.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:36.900
Another thing, deep within Gael.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:44.320
If you look really closely at his character model, he has a perfect circle that looks identical to the dark sigil.

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:47.300
Which is the mark that resembles the brand of the undead.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.080
And if you are hollow,

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:50.760
devoid of humanity,

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:56.000
Did you know that you will no longer cast a shadow upon the ground, or, a reflection in the water?

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:58.260
I think we can explain why this happens.

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:01.160
In the black flame item descriptions,

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:03.080
The, and I quote:

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:09.280
"Impenetrable flame of humanity is said to be a weighty physical force."

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:16.240
So, it makes some sense that, losing your soul, your humanity, would make a hollow more ethereal.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:21.180
and, thus they would be incapable of blocking out light and producing a shadow.

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:26.600
But, I'll admit, being shadowless is somewhat of a strange addition.

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:31.560
Especially considering it's never directly mentioned, and, out of all the Souls games

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:34.440
this, I believe only occurs in Dark Souls 3.

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:38.180
But, I can't really imagine them putting this in by mistake.

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:38.780
Can you?

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:44.320
Another thing, I'm always unsure of, is this interaction with the firekeeper.

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:49.560
So, it occurs when you return here, still drenched in the wax of the Grand Archives.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:53.480
She turns away, presumably in distaste.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:59.700
For, she does exactly the same thing when you wear one of the rings that mark you as someone from Londor .

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:04.260
And, as we all know, the hollows of Londor were widely detested.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:08.980
So, assumedly, she is turning away in distaste here as well.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:10.980
And, assuming this isn't a mistake:

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:11.860
Why?

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:15.880
Why would she turn away from a wax-headed scholar?

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:18.120
The only theory I have is this:

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:22.060
To a degree, Firelink Shrine functions as an extension of Lothric

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:27.960
A kingdom devoted to the linking of the fire, which is a goal that's upheld by the three pillars:

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:30.940
The Knight, The Priestess, and The Scholar.

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:38.260
And of the three, there is evidence that the scholars started to go against the knights and the priestesses.

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:41.260
And Lothric's firelinking legacy in general.

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:46.700
For example, the first of the scholars is said to have doubted the linking of the fire.

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:52.960
And, the blessed weapon enchantment was created after the scholars acquired the Grand Archives.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:58.460
Which, apparently marked the strengthening of ties between the other two pillars:

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:00.680
the Knights and the Handmaidens.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:05.080
So, it's quite possible that the scholars were the third pillar that were sort of

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:08.020
responsible for the fall of  entire structure.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:09.300
So to speak.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:15.200
And it's quite possible that this small, seemingly insignificant interaction, where she turns away

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:16.600
in disgust,

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:21.820
Could be, a third little nod towards the treachery of the scholars, as well.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:23.100
But that's just a theory.

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:29.540
And it's one of those things where it's really hard to know whether a detail is meant to be important from a lore perspective.

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:35.140
And, the same is definitely true when it comes to the pictures in the official design works.

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:39.220
Take, for example, this image of Filianore where she holds the egg.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:45.960
Except, the inside of this egg is overlayed with the stitched crystal lizard hide of a Transposing Kiln

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:48.980
Look how similar these two are.

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:53.400
So, the Transposing Kiln we find withing the Curse-Rotted Greatwood,

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:55.120
is said to hail from Courland

00:04:55.400 --> 00:05:01.440
And it's stitched with crystal lizard hide and it is capable of extracting the essence of a soul.

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:09.220
And, of course, the egg in game doesn't acctualy have this stitched crystal lizard hide transposing kiln within it

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:11.200
But still, even though this was changed,

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:17.180
the picture gives us this rare piece of insight into what the developers might have actually been thinking

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:19.140
when they designed Filianore.

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:23.480
It tells us, that at some stage, Filianor may have been linked with Courland.

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:28.560
And, that at some stage, the Transposing Kiln here may have been the method

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:32.160
by which the original Dark Soul was hidden within the Ringed City.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.840
Also notable in the design works,

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:39.560
Is a fourth shrine of Farron that doesn't appear alongside the three others in Farron swamp.

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:45.600
The three existing shrines depict the Four Kings, Nito, and the Witch of Izalith.

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:50.400
And this fourth, removed shrine, depicts Seath the Pale Dragon

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:54.460
The last three things I wanna talk about, are a few speedrunning tricks.

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:57.000
First, the fast wyvern kill.

00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:00.720
Basically, you run to the elevated part of the stairs

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:03.260
You hope, for the horizontal fire breath

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:06.340
And then you perform a jump attack with the right timing.

00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:07.820
And the fight's over.

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:10.660
Next, a jump-skip, to skip Irithyll

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:14.660
this one is best performed with a
keyboard, so that you can get some better

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:16.820
90-degree angle changes,

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:21.080
by nestling your
character in this corner, you align the camera just like this

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:26.140
then you sprint
into the corner and then abruptly run forward

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:31.680
and jump at the second step down.
From here if this short, glitchy walk to a

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:36.840
distant manor bonfire, which skips
basically all of Irithyll, to get to Yorm.

00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:41.700
And finally, a little trick that
completely immobilizes the watches of Faron

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:46.440
Walk into this corner, then align
your base vigor health bar,

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:49.580
just so it's at the edge near this candle,

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:51.580
then, tap forward on your keyboard,

00:06:51.860 --> 00:06:58.100
commit to a fully charged R2, then a single R2, 
skip the cutscene, quit out, get back in

00:06:58.440 --> 00:06:59.680
and the fight is yours.

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:03.620
So. I'm not going to
go into great detail on these,

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:08.040
because, honestly if these strats have piqued your interest in any way,

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:11.200
then you can find them all on the speed souls wiki

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:18.380
or you really should watch them all performed firsthand by the speedrunning community this game has on twitch

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:22.500
because if you haven't yet delved into
that side of the souls community

00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:23.400
Do it!

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:26.320
I've been waiting for an excuse to shot
them out for ages.

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:30.020
You can watch these streamers for hours on end and never get bored,

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:35.460
because it's so exciting watching them break the game in such controlled ways and you never know

00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:39.260
when they're about to break a new world record 
